# Cross-platform line-ending policy.
# Windows hosts should also set: git config --global core.autocrlf true
# Linux/macOS hosts should also set: git config --global core.autocrlf input
# That combination makes both surfaces store LF in git, with Windows checkouts
# getting CRLF on disk transparently. Prevents whip-saw when the same repo is
# touched from Cowork (Linux mount) and a Windows host on the same day.

# Default: detect text vs binary, normalise to LF on commit
* text=auto eol=lf

# Markdown / docs / config — LF (matches GitHub rendering and most editors)
*.md       text eol=lf
*.markdown text eol=lf
*.txt      text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.toml     text eol=lf

# Code / scripts that run on POSIX — LF
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
*.js 